    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d250">

                <pb facs="0384" n="282" sameAs="frus:frus1927v03/pg282"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862i.73/80</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Netherlands Minister</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Van Royen</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-11-02"><hi rendition="#italic">November 2,
                        1927</hi>.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to refer to this
                    Department’s note, dated March 14, 1927, and to your Legation’s <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Aide-Mémoire</hi>, dated June 24. 1927,<anchor n="13"
                        xml:id="d250-f1"/> concerning the proposed allocation of the Yap–Menado
                    cable to your Government in satisfaction of claims of its nationals in respect
                    to the German-Netherlands Telegraph Company.</p>
                <p>With respect to your Government’s claim that on account of the delay in
                    transferring the Yap–Menado, to the Netherlands, the sum of 2,388,671. marks
                    gold should be paid instead of the delivery of the cable,<anchor n="14"
                        xml:id="d250-f2"/> I regret to inform you that it has not been found
                    possible favorably to entertain that request. It is believed that the only
                    solution of the question is the delivery of the cable, as a full settlement of
                    the rights of Netherland nationals. An effort is being made to dispose of this
                    matter at a very early date.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Frank B. Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
